{"Handlers call deleteScheduledEmailReminder/deleteScheduledSMSReminder without awaiting or collecting the returned promises, so the request can finish before the DB update/delete executes and reminders may still be sent": 0.9580869674682617, "deleteScheduledEmailReminder with immediateDelete=true returns after a SendGrid call without updating/deleting the DB row, so the cron (which only processes cancelled=true) can't retry or clean up if the SendGrid call fails": 0.69931560754776, "scheduleEmailReminders calls @sendgrid/client.request to cancel scheduled sends but never calls client.setApiKey, so the cancellation requests can fail and cancelled reminders will remain scheduled": 0.18845827877521515, "The cron cancellation loop is wrapped in a single try/catch, so one SendGrid failure stops processing the rest and also skips deleting already-processed reminders from the DB": 0.9672412872314453}